# Autonomous execution (StreakBooks)

Gulshan (Operations) authorised routine autonomous development for `streakbooks/StreakBooks`, with hard limits below.

## May run without re-asking

- Read-only Git inspection and `git fetch` / `git pull --ff-only`
- `npm` / `npm.cmd` install, typecheck, lint, tests, builds, and `check:*` gates
- Stage and commit on **feature branches only**, after verifying branch + diff + relevant gates
- Push to non-protected feature remotes; create/update PRs; read Actions / CI logs
- Prefer short focused commands; do not bundle destructive ops with routine gates

## Always require explicit user authorization

- Merge to `main` / `master` (including `gh pr merge`)
- Admin merge overrides / bypassing branch protection or required reviews
- Force push and other destructive Git (`reset --hard`, discarding dirty work, etc.)
- Production DB migrations, production deploys, secrets or credential changes

## Before each commit

1. Confirm current branch is a feature branch (not `main`/`master`)
2. Review `git status` and staged/unstaged diff
3. Confirm relevant local gates for the change set
4. Commit only requested/verified work; never commit secrets

Project Auto-review steering lives in `.cursor/permissions.json` (`autoRun` only — no broad terminal allowlist).
